<!DOCTYPE suite SYSTEM "https://testng.org/testng-1.0.dtd">
<!-- Pure-HTTP API tests only — no WebDriver, no Selenium Grid, no browser. Deliberately
     listed as explicit <classes> rather than a <packages> scan (unlike the UI suites'
     package-scan pattern): a package scan would need every current and future class in
     com.automation.sites.demoqa.tests to be reviewed for whether it happens to need a
     browser, whereas an explicit list only ever runs what's named here, and stays correct
     by construction as new UI test classes are added to that package over time.

     Scoped to demoqa's API tests only (site-coupled: -Dsite=demoqa, the default) — see
     api-tests-jsonplaceholder.xml for the standalone API-only site's suite, kept as a
     SEPARATE file rather than a second <test> block in this one. Reason: -Dsite is a single
     JVM-wide system property (see ConfigReader's own class javadoc), so one `mvn test`
     invocation can only ever resolve one site's base URI — BookStoreApiTest needs
     -Dsite=demoqa and JsonPlaceholderApiTest needs -Dsite=jsonplaceholder, and there is no
     TestNG suite-XML construct that lets two <test> blocks in the same JVM run with two
     different values of the same system property. Splitting into two suite files (each run
     as its own `mvn test -Dsite=...` invocation) is what actually keeps both runnable
     correctly, rather than a single suite that only works for whichever site happens to be
     passed. See the "api-tests" CI job in github-ci.yml, which runs both suites as separate
     steps for exactly this reason.

     PARALLEL EXECUTION: classes + thread-count=2. Both classes here create their own
     disposable account and don't share any state (unlike BaseTest's ThreadLocal<WebDriver>
     UI tests need to worry about) — there's nothing about running them in parallel that's
     unsafe. Only two classes exist today, so thread-count=2 just means "run them both at
     once"; bump it if more demoqa API test classes are added later.

     WHY THIS SUITE EXISTS separately from demoqa-smoke.xml/demoqa-regression.xml, which
     already run these same classes via their group filter + package scan: those suites
     require the full Selenium/browser CI setup (ChromeDriver, the Docker Selenium Grid,
     browser matrix) to run at all, even though these two classes need none of it. This
     suite lets API tests run fast and standalone — see the "api-tests" CI job in
     github-ci.yml/.gitlab-ci.yml, which runs this suite directly on the base
     maven:...-eclipse-temurin-17 image with no browser/Grid setup step at all. -->
<suite name="API Tests Suite - demoqa" parallel="classes" thread-count="2">

  <!-- RetryListener is an IAnnotationTransformer — must be registered here
       (or via ServiceLoader), not via @Listeners on a test class, or it
       silently never fires. See BaseTest.java for the full explanation.
       Kept here too even though API failures are usually deterministic
       (a real contract violation, not browser flakiness) — a transient
       network blip hitting demoqa.com's API is exactly the kind of thing
       worth one retry before failing the build. -->
  <listeners>
    <listener class-name="com.automation.sites.listeners.RetryListener"/>
  </listeners>

  <test name="Book Store API Tests" preserve-order="true">
    <groups>
      <run>
        <include name="api"/>
      </run>
    </groups>

    <classes>
      <class name="com.automation.sites.demoqa.tests.BookStoreApiTest"/>
      <class name="com.automation.sites.demoqa.tests.BookStoreApiNegativeTest"/>
    </classes>

  </test>

</suite>
